        Cell[CellGroupData[
          {Cell["Stable numerical evaluation of the mixed derivative",
            "Subsection", ExpressionUUID ->
             "29d15b91-86a0-054b-af83-32c9fa67b545"], Cell["For F4, let F(z) \
= regularized 3F2({2 I nu,1/2-I nu,1};{1+z,1+z};1). Symmetry gives F4 = [z^2] \
F(z) - d_c^2 regularized 2F1(2 I nu,1/2-I nu;c;1)|c=1. The second term \
follows from Gauss summation. The first is evaluated by a discrete Cauchy \
integral on |z|=1/128. Sample count grows with requested precision; \
convergence and agreement with the original derivative are tested below. This \
evaluates an analytic parameter derivative, not a finite-regulator \
approximation to P.", "Text", ExpressionUUID ->
             "a9510dbb-8b4e-ee4c-bb51-5d1278aff660"],
           Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{RowBox[{"mixedMaster", "[",
                   RowBox[{RowBox[{"v_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",",
                     "prec_Integer", ",", RowBox[{"n_Integer", ":", "0"}]}],
                   "]"}], ":=", RowBox[{"Module", "[", RowBox[
                    {RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"vv", "=", RowBox[{"N",
                          "[", RowBox[{"v", ",", RowBox[{"prec", "+",
                          "20"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "a", ",", "b", ",",
                         RowBox[{"rad", "=", FractionBox["1", "128"]}], ",",
